{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_cache", "label": "Cache interface", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Seven operations cover ~95 % of real cases; the surface stays small on purpose - no pattern scans and no pub/sub, since the cluster has its own.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_opportunistic_semantics", "label": "Opportunistic cache semantics", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Caches are lossy by design: a None from get means 'not cached' and the caller must fall back to the source of truth; implementations return defaults on transient failures rather than throwing, while misuse throws.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_ttl_semantics", "label": "TTL semantics", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Entries without a TTL grow until eviction, so explicit TTLs are the predictable choice for most uses.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_incr", "label": "Atomic increment (incr)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Returns the new count and applies ttlMs only when the counter was just created, which is the right semantics for a fixed-window rate limiter.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_setifabsent", "label": "setIfAbsent (atomic compare-and-set)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Atomicity is a guarantee, not best effort: every backend maps it onto a single native CAS (Redis SET NX, Memcached ADD, an uninterruptible Map pair in-process), and ttlMs applies only to the winning write so a retry loop cannot extend someone else's hold.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_acquirelock", "label": "acquireLock (token-checked lock)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Writes a random 128-bit token and deletes only if that token is still there; the naive delete-in-finally evicts the next owner once a holder overruns its TTL. ttlMs is required because expiry is the only recovery path from a crashed holder. Not a consensus lock: release is a get then a delete, so a fencing token is needed where two holders would be a correctness bug.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_bulk_operations", "label": "Bulk operations (mget / mset)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Round-trip optimisation, critical for shared-entity hydration after a sharding rebalance - one call instead of N.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_instance_isolation", "label": "One cache instance per consumer", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A bounded cache evicts on recency alone, so an entry carrying a guarantee (rate-limit counter, idempotency record, lock) goes as readily as a cached response body; naming each consumer's cache stops a caller who enumerates one key space from reaching another's state.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at"